    """Align positions to Ior until both sources end, without truncating either side.

    Construction pulls nothing; each output pulls each live side once, left before right.
    Exhausted sides are never polled again. Left and Right denote source sides.
    State is constant-sized; move-only payloads, captures and origins are preserved.

    Parameters:
        A: The first callback argument type.
        B: The second callback argument type.
        V: The consumed native iterator or owned collection type.
        W: The second consumed source type.

    Args:
        source: The source, consumed at its current position.
        other: The second source, consumed at its current position.

    Returns:
        AlignIterator[A, B, _Source[V], _Source[W]] with the ownership, timing and empty-input behavior described above.
    """
    return _Align[A, B, _Source[V], _Source[W]](_source(source^), _source(other^), False, False)

def pad_zip[A: Movable & Deinitable, B: Movable & Deinitable, V: Movable & Deinitable, W: Movable & Deinitable](var source: V, var other: W) -> PadZipIterator[A, B, _Source[V], _Source[W]] where _Source[V].Element == A and _Source[W].Element == B:
    """Align positions to pairs of Optional fields, never yielding two absent fields.

    Construction pulls nothing; each output pulls each live side once, left before right.
    Exhausted sides are never polled again. Left and Right denote source sides.
    State is constant-sized; move-only payloads, captures and origins are preserved.

    Parameters:
        A: The first callback argument type.
        B: The second callback argument type.
        V: The consumed native iterator or owned collection type.
        W: The second consumed source type.

    Args:
        source: The source, consumed at its current position.
        other: The second source, consumed at its current position.

    Returns:
        PadZipIterator[A, B, _Source[V], _Source[W]] with the ownership, timing and empty-input behavior described above.
